1. Build a path where vertices with odd parity requirements appear an odd number of times
2. Vertices with even parity requirements appear an even number of times
3. Path length must be at most 4n
4. If no valid path exists, output -1

Key insight: In any path, vertices with odd visit counts must be visited an odd number of times (typically start/end points with possible revisits), while even parity vertices must be visited even times.

